  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a single, highly specific public housing complex in Naples, which may limit generalizability to other inhabited ruins or touristified social housing sites.",
      "what": "This study conceptualizes the Vele of Scampia, a public housing complex in Naples, Italy, as an inhabited ruin to examine how material decay and symbolic degradation shape residents' lives. It investigates how these residents perceive and navigate the presence of tourists who visit their marginalized neighborhood.",
      "why": "It reveals a paradox where tourism simultaneously offers visibility and social inclusion to a marginalized community while risking the reproduction of social stigma and feelings of otherness."
